@startuml uml-team-composition-flow
title PolyMarket Social ("Justify") — Team Composition as a Parallel Flow\n48 seats per team-composition.md; fork = work proceeding in parallel without blocking

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam partition {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #888888
}

' Activity color classes: phase0 = Phase-0 deliverable (blue),
' mvp = seat on the CEO MVP critical path (orange) — see legend.
' (Defaults live here too: a skinparam activity BackgroundColor would
' override the per-class styles below.)
<style>
activityDiagram {
  activity {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor #888888
    .phase0 {
      BackgroundColor #D6E8FF
    }
    .mvp {
      BackgroundColor #FFE6CC
    }
  }
}
</style>

start

partition "Phase 0 — bootstrap (the only serialized work, team-composition.md §4)" {
  fork
    :OpenAPI specs ×16\n(BE seats draft,\nARCH-1 arbitrates);<<phase0>>
  fork again
    :Solidity interfaces,\nevent catalog,\ncent/decimals conventions\n(ARCH-2 + SC-1..3);<<phase0>>
  fork again
    :Address artifact format,\nseed-market fixtures\n(SC-3 + QA-1);<<phase0>>
  fork again
    :DB schema namespace\nallocation\n(ARCH-1 + BP-1);<<phase0>>
  fork again
    :Gateway skeleton,\nservice scaffold,\nroute registry\n(BP-1);<<phase0>>
  fork again
    :Design tokens, layout\nshell, data-testid scheme\n(FE-1 + QA-7);<<phase0>>
  fork again
    :docker-compose: api,\nstorage, oauth-mock,\noracle-mock\n(DO-1);<<phase0>>
  end fork
  :Contract freeze (rule G2) — ARCH-1 signs off;\nlater changes only via change control (§11);
}

note right
  During Phase 0 the remaining seats are
  not idle: they work against the read-only
  prototype (G6) — page objects, component
  specs, visual styling — and draft their
  own contracts for review.
end note

fork
  partition "Group A — Architecture & coordination (5)" {
    fork
      :ARCH-1\nChief Architect\nchange control,\narbitration;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :ARCH-2\nBlockchain\nArchitect;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :ARCH-3\nTest Strategy\nArchitect;
    fork again
      :ARCH-4\nRepo Architect\nownership matrix;
    fork again
      :ARCH-5\nArchitecture\nReviewer (audits);
    end fork
  }
fork again
  partition "Group B — Smart contracts (3)" {
    fork
      :SC-1\nMarketFactory,\nPredictionMarket,\nOracleResolver;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :SC-2\nMarketAMM,\nOutcomeToken,\nMockUSDC;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :SC-3\nFeeTreasury,\nAccessControl,\nmigrations + seeding;<<mvp>>
    end fork
  }
fork again
  partition "Group C — Backend (17)" {
    fork
      :BP-1\nGateway &\nplatform;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :BE-1\nAuth API;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :BE-2\nWallet\nAuth API;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :BE-3\nUsers API;
    fork again
      :BE-4\nPosts API;
    fork again
      :BE-5\nComments\nAPI;
    fork again
      :BE-6\nEngagement\nAPI;
    fork again
      :BE-7\nSocial\nGraph API;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :BE-8\nMarkets API;
    fork again
      :BE-9\nMarket\nCreation API;
    fork again
      :BE-10\nOrders API;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :BE-11\nMarket\nData API;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :BE-12\nPortfolio\nAPI;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :BE-13\nNotifications\nAPI;
    fork again
      :BE-14\nSearch API;
    fork again
      :BE-15\nMedia API;
    fork again
      :BE-16\nSupport API;
    end fork
  }
fork again
  partition "Group D — Web client (10)" {
    fork
      :FE-1\nLayout shell,\ndesign tokens;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :FE-2\nMarket-card\nwidget;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :FE-3\nAuth client;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :FE-4\nWallet\nconnector;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :FE-5\nFeed page;
    fork again
      :FE-6\nMarkets\npage;
    fork again
      :FE-7\nTrading\npage;
    fork again
      :FE-8\nPortfolio\npage;
    fork again
      :FE-9\nProfile &\nsettings;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :FE-10\nSecondary\npages;
    end fork
  }
fork again
  partition "Group E — QA & test automation (11)" {
    fork
      :QA-1\nTest infra,\nfixtures;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :QA-2\nIT: auth,\nusers;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :QA-3\nIT: social;
    fork again
      :QA-4\nIT: markets,\ntrading;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :QA-5\nIT: portfolio,\nsupport;
    fork again
      :QA-6\nIT: cross-API\nflows;
    fork again
      :QA-7\nE2E framework,\npage objects;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :QA-8\nE2E journeys\nJ1–J8;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :QA-9\nE2E component\nspecs;
    fork again
      :QA-10\nGenerator:\nnews, templating;
    fork again
      :QA-11\nGenerator:\nlifecycle, safety;
    end fork
  }
fork again
  partition "Group F — DevOps & CI (2)" {
    fork
      :DO-1\nCompose\nenvironment;<<mvp>>
    fork again
      :DO-2\nCI pipelines,\nrelease gates;<<mvp>>
    end fork
  }
end fork

:Integration checkpoints (§11) — QA-6 cross-API flows and QA-8 journeys:\nthe first place contract drift between unblocked seats becomes visible;

:MVP gate — CEO-1..4 green via Tier-1 journeys J1, J5, J2/J3\n(functional-requirements-ceo.md §2; ui-testing.md §5);\nhardcode-fallback areas ship as the prototype renders them (CEO §3);

stop

legend bottom
  Flow view of team-composition.md. Forks denote work that proceeds in
  parallel; the only serialized stretch is Phase 0, which freezes the
  contracts (OpenAPI, Solidity interfaces, schema namespaces, fixtures)
  that decouple every cross-seat dependency (§7). After the freeze all
  48 seats run concurrently under the single-writer rule (G1).
  Colors — blue: Phase-0 deliverables; orange: seats on the CEO MVP
  critical path (§8, about 22 of 48; BE-1/BE-2 and FE-3/FE-4 are
  "at least one of" alternatives); white: seats whose areas may ship
  hardcoded per functional-requirements-ceo.md §3.
  The joins are checkpoints, not hard barriers: integration probes run
  continuously as seats land work; the MVP gate blocks release only on
  the Tier-1 journeys.
endlegend

@enduml
